1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Until you type your payday, Auto shows this sample plan.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:13,000
This Paycheck is made for your phone. It shows the next payday, the bills that check pays, and Left after bills.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,500
The Dashboard shows the same next check, Left after bills, and a per-day figure.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:28,000
This sample check pays rent, car insurance, streaming and the car payment.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,500
Left after bills is what remains after bills, one-time costs and living money. Below zero means SHORT.

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Per day until next payday spreads that leftover across the days the check has to cover.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,500
The heads-up line names the next short check, so you can fix it early.

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:00,000
The leftover chart of your next 12 checks. SHORT bars sit below zero.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,500
Your next 6 checks, at a glance.

10
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:13,000
Paycheck Plan looks ahead up to 52 paychecks. Each row is one check.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,500
Check Detail lists every bill one check pays. Type any check number from 1 to 52.

12
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:28,000
Bill Calendar lays bills, paydays and one-time costs on a month grid. Nothing to type.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Next chapter: fixing a short check.
